  "final_message": "The notification center is built, but I haven't run the Docker image because Docker isn't available in this sandbox. I did run the Flask API through its test client and it behaved as specified. That covered register, login, create, read and unread, read-all, delete, broadcast, and another user getting a 404 on your notification. The frontend builds (`npm run build` passes `tsc` and `vite build`), but I haven't opened it in a browser.\n\n**Backend (`backend/app.py`):**\n- Every endpoint in your list is there, plus `POST /api/auth/logout` and `GET /api/auth/me`, which the frontend uses.\n- Passwords are hashed, and tokens expire after 7 days.\n- Registering `admin` returns 409, and admin sign-in is off unless `ADMIN_PASSWORD` is set.\n- Usernames are case-insensitive: `Alice` can't register if `alice` exists.\n- Broadcast also lands in the admin's own inbox, and the admin's `delivered` count includes it.\n- An oversized `page_size` is capped at 100 rather than rejected, and `type` defaults to `info` (or `announcement` for a broadcast).\n- SQLite lives at `data/notifications.db`. The path can be overridden with `DATA_DIR`.\n\n**Frontend (`frontend/src`):** It has sign-in and register forms, the username with a sign-out button, a bell with the unread count, and the inbox with filters, per-item toggles, delete and paging. The add-notification form is there, and the broadcast form shows only for the admin. It's styled with Tailwind utility classes only. Messages render as plain text.\n\n**Other changes:**\n- I added Tailwind, TypeScript and the React type packages to `frontend/package.json` at pinned versions and updated the lock file.\n- The build script is now `tsc && vite build`.\n- I added a `.gitignore`.",
